  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 222 PM MDT WED SEP 16 2026\nThe upper low will shift eastward out of our area on Saturday, \ncontinuing remnant isolated showers/thunderstorms over the \neasternmost portions of our CWA. Otherwise, high pressure will \nrebuild over the western US by Sunday, bringing a slight warming\nand drying trend to the region through midweek. Temperatures \nwill reach back to near seasonal normals, with highs in the low \n80s for the Treasure Valley Monday through Tuesday. Tuesday \nthrough Wednesday, there is considerable guidance uncertainty \nover how far a longwave trough steering into western BC extends \ndown into the northwest region. There is slight potential for \nthe central ID mountains to see precipitation late Tuesday into \nWednesday, as well as a slight area-wide cooldown. Otherwise, \nthe area will stay mostly dry and warm through midweek.",
